## Purpose

Stores human-written notes attached to an applicant throughout the review process. These notes provide context that should not be generated or overwritten by automated AI analysis.

Examples include observations, escalation reasons, manual decisions, and internal reviewer comments.

---

## Table Relationships

| Relationship | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `intake_id` → `intake.intake_id` | Each note belongs to a single applicant. |
| One applicant | Can have multiple notes. |

---

# Columns

## Identity

| Column | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `id` | Unique note identifier (UUID). |
| `intake_id` | Applicant the note belongs to. |

---

## Author Information

| Column | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `author_id` | User or reviewer who created the note. |

---

## Note Content

| Column | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `note_text` | The actual note content. |
| `note_type` | Category of note for filtering and reporting. |

Allowed values:

| Value | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `observation` | General reviewer observation. |
| `flag_reason` | Reason an applicant was flagged. |
| `escalation_reason` | Reason the application was escalated. |
| `decision_note` | Explanation for an acceptance/rejection or other decision. |

---

## Audit

| Column | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `created_at` | Timestamp when the note was created. |

---

# Constraints

### Primary Key

```
id
```

---

### Foreign Key

```
intake_id
    ↓
intake.intake_id
```

Each note must reference an existing applicant.

---

### Check Constraint

`note_type` is restricted to:

- observation
- flag_reason
- escalation_reason
- decision_note

---

# Typical Workflow

```
Applicant

↓

Manual Review

↓

Reviewer adds note

↓

Applicant profile displays note history

↓

Future reviewers can see previous decisions
```

---

# Common Use Cases

- Document why an applicant was rejected.
- Explain why an application was escalated.
- Record manual observations during review.
- Leave handoff notes for another recruiter or scout.
- Maintain an audit trail of human decisions.